{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-09-12T19:57:58.972Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-1","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"ef0a31908b232616bff09378","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-1","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.269","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-8eclqf"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"pm get --json omits the whole item as budget-infeasible when its standard projection exceeds the default ceiling although the contract's own brief depth fits, so one active item is unreadable by default"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"## Observed\npm get pm-5t33or --json exits 2 with output_budget_exceeded.reason requested_budget_infeasible and omits the whole item, while pm get pm-5t33or (TOON), --depth brief and --depth deep all succeed, and --output-budget 20000 succeeds. The item's full JSON is 31,218 bytes (about 7.8k estimated tokens) against the default 6,000-token ceiling; it has 26 dependencies, a 2,725-character description and a 1,111-character body, no notes and no comments. The refusal receipt reports estimated_tokens 177 and within_budget false, so the number shown is the receipt's own size rather than the omitted result's.\n\n## Population\nProbed every active item on 2026-09-12: 308 of 309 open and draft items read at the default budget; pm-5t33or is the only refusal. The shape is rare today and structural: any single-entity read whose standard projection exceeds the ceiling has no degradation step between full standard and omit everything, although the contract declares brief as a cheaper amount dimension for the same command.\n\n## Why it matters\npm get is the command an agent uses to rebuild an item; a default read that refuses outright is the one outcome the output-budget feature pm-5t33or exists to prevent (degrade deterministically instead of emitting unbounded output). pm-3crymx closed the same receipt defect for context; this is its shape on get.\n\n## Non-goals\nNot a change to the default ceiling. Not linked files/tests/docs projection (pm-tld20c, closed)."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","area:sdk","get","output-budget","read-output","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-09-12T19:57:58.972Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-12T19:57:58.972Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The single-entity degradation ladder steps standard to brief before omission and the receipt records the applied depth and the reason; The refusal receipt reports the omitted result's estimated tokens, never the receipt's own size; A probe over every active item returns exit 0 at the default budget, with a negative control for an item whose brief projection also exceeds the ceiling; A spec reproduces pm-5t33or's shape: 26 dependencies and a 2,700-character description under the default budget"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5t33or"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A single-entity read whose standard projection exceeds the ceiling degrades to the declared brief projection and reports the applied depth; the receipt's estimated_tokens names the omitted result's size."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"pm get pm-5t33or --json exits 2 requested_budget_infeasible with estimated_tokens 177 while --depth brief, --depth deep, TOON and --output-budget 20000 all succeed."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-3crymx","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-09-12T19:57:58.972Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-j82fd3","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-09-12T19:57:58.972Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"ec54905af9488f9adaf6400bf9ab44e9e84b3e627646033d598c331264001c00","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"c934b575cab0204acdb297753b306f5adcca4d42696e6c902c1d3c4ef4d6c3af"}
